[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise. The desk
merged them by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and many
different subjects can describe one bug while one subject can describe two. This page counts by
what each report shows, so every problem gets its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row. The other rows need fixes of their own, and
until they ship, those reports keep coming in.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. Day and month come out swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. Any channel. Fix: parse
  with the tenant's locale.
- **`hint`**: same swap, different bug. The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date
  field, so the tenant's people type month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way. Only
  form reports from tenants on booking-v3. The parser fix does not touch it. Fix: print the
  tenant's own order under the field.
- **`shift`**: not a swap at all. The date lands **one day early**: Tuesday 12 May shows as
  Monday 11 May, a client in Toronto gets Monday while Lisbon gets Tuesday, an invite arrives
  before the booking was made. A date stored as midnight and shown in a zone west of it. The
  desk read these right (`oneDayMove` in `desk-notes.json`), and the cause table still counts
  them under `parser` by tenant: R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620.

## What the cause table shows

The cause table on #4471 places a report by tenant and channel only. It cannot see what a body
says, so it folds the one-day reports into `parser` and leaves them as a footnote:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. Check the other rows first.
- New reports with a one-day move go to the `shift` ticket, not here.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. Place by tenant, channel and body.

